From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Multisampling and temporal anti-aliasing

Opt-in multisampling (OpenGL/multisampling in Webots' preferences,
default 0): opaque geometry drawn multisampled, alpha-masked materials
with alpha to coverage, resolved before ambient occlusion.

Temporal anti-aliasing (OpenGL/temporalAntiAliasing, on): the main view
jitters its projection by a sub-pixel Halton offset each frame and
blends the frame (HDR, after the fog) with its history reprojected
through depth: a Catmull-Rom history, clamped to the neighbourhood's
range, rejected where its stored depth disagrees (surfaces revealed
behind moving foliage), taking more of the new frame in motion. Robot
cameras stay single-frame.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0025-multisampling: at 4 samples, foliage flicker -31%, frame +9.4 ms
- 0041-temporal-anti-aliasing: needles flickering under a quarter-pixel
  turn 3.9% -> 0.36% of canopy pixels; +1.5% frame time
